summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Follow-up for IBS with functional abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Brittany Edwards is a 32-year-old female who is a return visit for IBS with functional abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting. The patient was last seen in 08/2019 with flares of abdominal pain, who was diagnosed with Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) and was treated with Bentyl. She had a previous prescription for Reglan that she received from the emergency room that she used as needed for nausea. She was instructed to start a low dose fiber supplement, such as Citrucel, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, Bentyl up to 4 times daily for intestinal cramping, and stop Reglan and use Zofran as needed. Neuromodulators such as Elavil and Buspar were discussed but not started.

The patient states she has been going out to eat on Friday nights and Saturday nights and that she has had some spicy foods or spicy shrimp. She reports she does not like spicy food at all. She reports that she is starting to notice bowel movement between 2 and 3 times a day. The patient states she is avoiding heavy foods due to cramping and sharp pains. She reports she did have some fried chicken today and was okay.

The patient states that she does not eat out daily. She states that she does go out to eat with friends sometimes. The patient states she usually eats pasta, chicken alfredo at Friday's. She states that she usually does not have any issues with this. The patient states she prefers to drink Patron, but if she gets brown liquor, she only gets two. She states she only drinks out every now and then. She states she will drink a martini every now and then. The patient states she does not have issues with this.

The patient states she is not using Citrucel regularly. The patient states she needs to find a new drink.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Negative for fever, chills, or unintentional weight loss.
Gastrointestinal: Positive for diarrhea, nausea, and abdominal pain.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.
Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm.
Abdomen: Soft, non-tender. No masses or organomegaly. Normal active bowel sounds.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Ms. Brittany Edwards is a pleasant, 32-year-old female who presents for follow-up for IBS and functional abdominal pain, aggravated by high stress, poor eating habits, and poor sleeping habits. I have encouraged dietary and lifestyle modifications, as well as starting a neuromodulator such as Elavil 25 mg at bedtime for IBS. She can use Bentyl 20 mg as needed 30 to 45 minutes prior to eating out at a restaurant. She can also use Zofran if needed. However, I have encouraged her to reduce greasy and fatty foods and alcohol consumption. I have asked her to follow up in 1 month by email regarding any side effects and issues, or issues with Elavil or if adjustments are needed.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 1 month. }}<|eot_id|>
