Right knee pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Tyler Nelson is a 73-year-old male who presents today for the management of his rheumatoid arthritis. He last received a steroid injection in his right knee and reports that the injection provided relief for approximately 2 weeks. The patient states that his pain level is about 6 out of 10 on a normal day. He also reports that his right knee has been swollen for the past 2 months. He notes that he has been wearing compression socks to help with the swelling. The patient states that the swelling has not improved with the use of compression socks. The patient reports that he has been limited in his activities and requires the use of a cane to aid in ambulation.

The patient reports that he is taking Xeljanz 11 mg daily and Celebrex 200 mg daily, which he started 2 months ago. He states that he is compliant with his medication regimen.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports that he enjoys salty snacks.

MEDICATIONS

Xeljanz 11 mg daily
Celebrex 200 mg daily

PHYSICAL EXAM

CV: Normal capillary refill in the toes.
MS: Right knee: Pitting edema around the knee and ankle. Range of motion slightly diminished. Increased heat to the right knee.

ASSESSMENT

1. Rheumatoid arthritis with right knee involvement.
2. Edema, etiology to be determined.

PLAN

After reviewing the patient's examination and radiographic findings, I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient in regards to his current symptoms. I have recommended that we proceed with another right knee steroid injection. The patient was administered a right knee steroid injection today. We have also ordered an X-ray of the right knee to evaluate the underlying cause of the edema. Additionally, we will start the patient on physical therapy. If his symptoms do not improve, we will consider a surgical consult.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up with his PCP for the right knee steroid injection. The patient will follow up with me for the X-ray results. The patient will also follow up with me in 2 months for his Xeljanz level check. }}<|eot_id|>
