summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Left knee pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Angela Rodriguez is a pleasant 28-year-old female who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of left knee pain. The onset of her pain began 1 week ago when she was playing with her 5-year-old niece. She states she felt a pop in her left knee at the time of injury. She has been limping since the injury. She rates her pain as a 4 out of 10. The pain is constant and it has not improved. She denies hearing a pop in the knee. She states she is unable to bear weight on the left leg. She has been taking Tylenol and wrapping her knee with kinesiology tape. Her previous doctor advised her to avoid NSAIDs due to a ulcer history.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Musculoskeletal: Reports left knee pain.

VITALS

Vitals are within normal limits.

PHYSICAL EXAM

MSK: Examination of the left knee: Edema present, effusion present, moderate range of motion, pain with flexion and extension, negative Lachman's test, negative valgus and varus test.

RESULTS

X-ray of the left knee was obtained today and was normal. No fractures or bony abnormalities were noted.

ASSESSMENT

Left knee pain, likely MCL strain.

PLAN

After reviewing the patient's examination and radiographic findings today, I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient in regards to her current symptoms. I have explained to the patient that her x-ray was normal, which is a good thing. Her symptoms are consistent with an MCL strain. I have recommended that we treat her conservatively. I have recommended that she wear a knee immobilizer for the next week. I have also recommended that she ice her knee 3-4 times a day for 20-30 minutes at a time. She will also take Tramadol 50 mg, 1 tablet orally, 2 times a day for pain. She can take Tylenol as needed for breakthrough pain. She should avoid running for the next 3 weeks.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up with me in 1 month if her symptoms do not improve. If her symptoms worsen, she should contact the office and we will consider obtaining an MRI of her left knee. }}<|eot_id|>
